.next/
node_modules/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.env*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
certificates/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/

# ML data and generated model artifacts
data/*
models/*
artifacts/
checkpoints/
wandb/

# The trained ranker is the exception: it cannot be rebuilt from a clone. Its
# training inputs are the label pool (photographs of real people, ignored
# below) and the 7.8 GB Fashion144k teacher pool, so `train_ranker.py` is only
# runnable by whoever holds those locally. At 29 KB the artifact is committed
# so that a fresh clone scores. Its embedding caches stay ignored — they are
# training scratch, and nothing in the service reads them.
!models/ranker/
models/ranker/*
!models/ranker/ranker.npz
!models/ranker/ranker.json

# The browser detector's model is a pinned, vendored dependency rather than a
# training artifact, and the WASM runtime beside it is useless without it.
!apps/web/public/mediapipe/models/
!apps/web/public/mediapipe/models/**

# Leaderboard store (per-machine game records)
.data/
# Labelling station. The photo pool is bulk local data; the collected
# decisions are the dataset itself — hours of irreplaceable human judgement
# and what the scoring model trains on — so they are tracked.
# `data/*` above excludes the tree's contents while leaving the directory
# traversable, so these negations can match.
apps/web/public/label-pool/
!data/labelling/
data/labelling/*
!data/labelling/*.jsonl

# Fashion144k: 7.8 GB teacher image pool, downloaded not committed.
data/fashion144k/

# Raw photo exports of the labelling pool. The ingested pool is already ignored
# above; these are the same photographs of real people, one step earlier, and
# must not reach the repository either.
/uqcs hackathon*/
/uqcs hackathon*.zip
